tion judgment\"},\"feedback\":null,\"instruction\":\"Read only useful passages. Notes and all-page cleanup are optional.\",\"literal_answer_contract\":{\"origin\":\"explicit experiment configuration, not inferred from question\",\"prefix\":\"\",\"suffix\":\"\"},\"phase\":\"RESEARCH\",\"remaining\":{\"action_slots\":173,\"backend_calls\":49,\"model_calls\":2,\"output_reservation\":44574},\"research_workflow\":{\"active_gap_not_verified\":null,\"available_pages_not_ranked_for_relevance\":[{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d264\"},\"ref\":\"d264\",\"snippet\":\" ... star a single Asian in a leading male role. \\\"Grey's Anatomy\\\" showed the romances of six white characters – exclusively with other white people – and betwee\",\"title\":\"https://veskocholakov.com/blog/2450\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d263\"},\"ref\":\"d263\",\"snippet\":\" ... Jodie Comer is a multi-talented superstar, it's just a shame the show can't seem to commit to her character's queer love story.\\n\\n22. Cristina Yang, Grey's \",\"title\":\"https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/a39556965/greatest-female-tv-characters-21st-century/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d262\"},\"ref\":\"d262\",\"snippet\":\" ... Tim Robbins and Susan Sarandon\\n\\nSusan Sarandon won her first Oscar for her leading role in Dead Man Walking while her partner at the time, Tim Robbins, was\",\"title\":\"https://ew.com/oscars/oscar-couples-nominated-same-year/?srsltid=AfmBOooNKSbMtK-snkBLQqcWHXj9EoeLtOez5uym_V7Caz6sM-3dVLm7\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d261\"},\"ref\":\"d261\",\"snippet\":\" ... Hugo's stories of Tinseltown in the 50s, 60s and 80s change Grant's perspective.\\n\\nWool\\n\\nRebecca Ferguson and Tim Robbins are set to star in Apple's series \",\"title\":\"https://variety.com/feature/books-becoming-movies-tv-sh